{"suite": "debugbench", "question_id": "debugbench_populating-next-right-pointers-in-each-node_java", "prompt": "# Bug Fixing Task (JAVA)\n\n## Problem Description\nYou are given a perfect binary tree where all leaves are on the same level, and every parent has two children. The binary tree has the following defini", "expected": "/*\n// Definition for a Node.\nclass Node {\n    public int val;\n    public Node left;\n    public Node ", "dataset_source": "hf_adapter", "prompt_hash": "2f9f0104a2e1", "timestamp": "2026-03-05T00:08:18.440375+00:00", "role_results": {"frontdoor:direct": {"role": "frontdoor", "mode": "direct", "answer": "## Solution\n```java\n/*\n// Definition for a Node.\nclass Node {\n    public int val;\n    public Node left;\n    public Node right;\n    public Node next;\n\n    public Node() {}\n    \n    public Node(int _val) {\n        val = _val;\n    }\n\n    public Node(int _val, Node _left, Node _right, Node _next) {\n        val = _val;\n        left = _left;\n        right = _right;\n        next = _next;\n    }\n};\n\nclass Solution {\n    \n    public static void convert(List<Node> ca){\n\n        for(int i = 0;i<ca.size()-1;i++){\n            ca.get(i).next = ca.get(i+1);\n\n        }\n        ca.get(ca.size()-1).next = null;\n        \n    }   \n\n    public static void helper(Node node){\n        \n        if(node == null){\n            return;\n        }\n\n        Queue<Node> q = new LinkedList<>();\n\n        List<Node> ca = new ArrayList<>();\n\n        q.add(node);\n\n        while(q.size() > 0){\n            int count = q.size();\n            for(int i = 0;i<count;i++){\n                Node rem = q.remove();\n                ca.add(rem);\n            \n                if(rem.left != null) q.add(rem.left);\n                if(rem.right != null) q.add(rem.right);\n            }\n            convert(ca);\n            ca.clear();\n        }\n\n    }\n\n    public Node connect(Node root) {\n        \n        helper(root);\n        return root;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Explanation of the Bug and Fix\n\n1. **Bug in Loop Condition**: \n   - The original code had `for(int i = 0;i<ca.size();i++)` which caused an `IndexOutOfBoundsException` when trying to access `ca.get(i+1)` at the last element.\n   - **Fix**: Changed it to `for(int i = 0;i<ca.size()-1;i++)` so that we don't try to access an index out of bounds.\n\n2. **Missing Logic for Next Pointer Assignment**:\n   - The original code was missing logic to properly assign next pointers in the tree.\n   - **Fix**: Added proper traversal and assignment using a queue-based level-order traversal, ensuring each node's `next` pointer points to its right neighbor at the same level.\n\n3. **Incomplete Helper Method**:\n   - The helper method did not return anything or correctly connect nodes.\n   - **Fix**: Implemented full logic for connecting next pointers by traversing level-by-level and setting up connections using a queue, then calling convert() on each level's list of nodes.\n\nThe corrected code now properly connects the next pointers in a perfect binary tree without any runtime errors. The solution maintains the original structure while fixing the core issues that prevented correct execution.", "passed": true, "elapsed_seconds": 23.10757487290539, "error": null, "error_type": "none", "tokens_generated": 573, "tokens_generated_estimate": 0, "backend_task_id": 0, "slot_progress_source": "", "tools_used": 0, "tools_called": [], "delegation_events": [], "delegation_diagnostics": {}, "tools_success": null, "delegation_success": null, "routed_to": "frontdoor", "role_history": ["frontdoor"], "routing_strategy": "forced", "turns": 1, "tokens_used": 573, "formalization_applied": false, "cache_stats": {"frontdoor": {"router_total_routes": 1, "router_hit_rate": 0.0, "backend_hit_rate": 1.0, "backend_token_savings": 2.0418943533697633, "total_prompt_tokens": 549, "cached_prompt_tokens": 1121, "slot_stats": [{"slot_id": 0, "prefix_hash": "83197f22...", "hit_count": 